 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2490) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2490) 'How the board picks its work
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:14Z (RFD66606-2490) 'The board picks work the way Hamming's "You and Your Research" (1986,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:15Z (RFD66606-2490) 'https://www.cs.virginia.edu/~robins/YouAndYourResearch.html) says a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-2490) 'researcher does (operator, 2026-11-25).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-2490) '- A problem is important when it has a reasonable attack. A problem
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:18Z (RFD66606-2490) '  with no attack is a non-goal, however large its consequence.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:19Z (RFD66606-2490) '- The beta's important problem is the one the gate of RFD66606-2436
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-2490) '  holds. Each session says which important problem its work serves and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-2490) '  what its attack is.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-2490) '- A session whose work serves no important problem stops or changes
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-2490) '  its goal, whatever work it has already started.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Doors stay open. A session says what it works on and what it needs,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-2490) '  and reads what the others say.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-2490) '- A slice of the effort goes to the bigger question: is the gate still
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-2490) '  the important problem?
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Unknowns stay on the page. Each RFD's "What is not known" and each
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-2490) '  planted-defect control is the list of evidence against the work.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Work is done so that others can build on it. A document comes before
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-2490) '  the code.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written
